{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "22", "m": "08", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "00", "M": "33", "S": "13"}}, "news": [{"title": "LiDAR mapping to plug property tax leakages in Trichy", "para": "The Trichy Corporation is set to launch its inaugural GIS mapping initiative, leveraging state-of-the-art drone technology. This extensive survey aims to uncover discrepancies in property tax assessments and mitigate revenue losses. Additionally, it will create a detailed database for improved urban planning. The corporation will accurately track assets such as roads, parks, and streetlights. The mapping will also play a vital role in evaluating green cover and facilitating afforestation efforts.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/technology/lidar-mapping-to-plug-property-tax-leakages-in-trichy/133393747?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-476244/133393747.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "technology"}, {"title": "Goa government to launch housing scheme during Diwali", "para": "Goa government will launch a chief minister's housing scheme for homeless citizens.  The scheme will provide affordable homes on a lease basis to eligible original Goans.  Strict residency criteria will ensure original residents without homes receive housing.  The Goa Housing Board will also pursue joint ventures for construction projects.  This initiative aims to provide peaceful living spaces until beneficiaries can purchase their own homes.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/residential/goa-government-to-launch-housing-scheme-during-diwali/133393720?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-30522/133393720.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "residential"}, {"title": "Nirman-2 delays stall building approvals, Credai tells Belagavi civic body", "para": "Credai Belagavi has urged the Belagavi City Corporation to expedite the renewal process for engineer licenses. Due to ongoing portal delays, many licensed engineers face challenges in submitting building permission applications. This delay adversely affects builders, engineers, and citizens in need of essential approvals. They specifically requested quicker renewals for alteration and G+4 permissions, ensuring improved civic service delivery and reducing potential disruptions.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/industry/nirman-2-delays-stall-building-approvals-credai-tells-belagavi-civic-body/133393560?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-136654/133393560.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "industry"}]}